/*
Detection Rule: AWS S3 Bucket Public Exposure via Policy or ACL Change
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1530 - Data from Cloud Storage
              T1098 - Account Manipulation
Severity: Critical
Description: Detects when an S3 bucket is intentionally or accidentally exposed
to the public via bucket policy changes granting Principal "*", ACL changes
setting public-read/write, disabling Block Public Access settings, or deletion
of a restrictive bucket policy. Attackers may intentionally expose buckets
containing sensitive data as a data extortion tactic or to stage exfiltration
without using their own credentials.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    eventSource="s3.amazonaws.com"
    eventName IN (
        "PutBucketPolicy", "PutBucketAcl",
        "DeleteBucketPolicy", "PutBucketPublicAccessBlock"
    )
    errorCode=""

| eval actor=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval bucket_name=requestParameters.bucketName
| eval bucket_acl=requestParameters.AccessControlPolicy.AccessControlList.Grant.Grantee.URI
| eval policy_doc=requestParameters.bucketPolicy
| eval public_access_cfg=requestParameters.PublicAccessBlockConfiguration

/* Detect specific public exposure conditions */
| eval public_acl=if(
    match(bucket_acl, "AllUsers|AuthenticatedUsers"), 1, 0)

| eval public_policy=if(
    match(policy_doc, "\"Principal\"\s*:\s*\"\*\"") OR
    match(policy_doc, "\"Principal\"\s*:\s*\{\"AWS\"\s*:\s*\"\*\"\}"),
    1, 0)

| eval block_public_disabled=if(
    eventName="PutBucketPublicAccessBlock" AND (
        match(public_access_cfg, "\"BlockPublicAcls\"\s*:\s*false") OR
        match(public_access_cfg, "\"BlockPublicPolicy\"\s*:\s*false")),
    1, 0)

| eval policy_deleted=if(eventName="DeleteBucketPolicy", 1, 0)

| where public_acl=1 OR public_policy=1 OR block_public_disabled=1 OR policy_deleted=1

| eval exposure_type=case(
    public_acl=1,            "Public ACL Applied",
    public_policy=1,         "Public Bucket Policy Applied",
    block_public_disabled=1, "Block Public Access Disabled",
    policy_deleted=1,        "Bucket Policy Deleted")

/* Score based on exposure type and whether write access is granted */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(public_policy=1 AND match(policy_doc,"s3:PutObject"), risk_score+70, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(public_acl=1 AND match(bucket_acl,"AllUsers"),        risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(public_policy=1,                                      risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(block_public_disabled=1,                              risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(policy_deleted=1,                                     risk_score+35, risk_score)

| stats
    count                    AS event_count,
    values(exposure_type)    AS exposure_types,
    values(bucket_name)      AS buckets_exposed,
    values(sourceIPAddress)  AS source_ips,
    values(awsRegion)        AS regions,
    min(_time)               AS first_seen,
    max(_time)               AS last_seen
    by actor, risk_score

| eval alert_title="S3 Bucket Public Exposure: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, exposure_types, buckets_exposed,
        source_ips, regions, event_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- Known public buckets: Maintain an exclusion list for intentionally public assets
- Dev account suppression: Scope the rule to production account IDs only
- policy_deleted severity: Reduce risk weight for policy deletions in sandbox accounts
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(bucket_name, "public-assets|static-web|cdn-|open-data")
  | where NOT match(userIdentity.accountId, "<dev-account-id>|<sandbox-account-id>")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Intentionally public S3 static website buckets (CloudFront origins, direct hosting)
- Open-source distribution buckets or public artifact repositories
- Development and sandbox accounts with intentionally relaxed policies
- AWS CloudFormation deploying public bucket configurations as defined in templates

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Immediately verify current bucket accessibility: aws s3api get-bucket-policy
   and aws s3api get-bucket-acl to confirm exposure status
2. Identify the data classification of the bucket contents
3. Check if any objects were publicly accessed after the policy change (S3 access logs)
4. Re-enable S3 Block Public Access and restore the restrictive policy immediately
5. If data was accessed publicly, treat all bucket contents as potentially compromised
6. Initiate data breach assessment if PII, PHI, or regulated data was exposed

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Current bucket policy: | makeresults | eval cmd="aws s3api get-bucket-policy
  --bucket <bucket_name>" (run via Lambda or Systems Manager for real-time check)
- Public access after policy change: index=aws_s3_access bucket=<bucket_name>
  httpStatus=200 requester="-" earliest=<first_seen> | stats count by key, remoteip
- Actor activity before exposure: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.userName=<actor> earliest=-2h latest=<first_seen>
  | table _time, eventName, requestParameters, sourceIPAddress

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events, S3 management events)
- S3 Server Access Logs (for post-exposure access detection)

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Exposure event followed immediately by high volume of anonymous GetObject requests
- Policy grants s3:PutObject to Principal: * (write-accessible public bucket)
- Actor made the change outside business hours or from an unknown IP
- Bucket name contains keywords: backup, data, db, export, confidential, internal

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Enable S3 Block Public Access at the AWS Organization and account level by default
- Apply SCP: Deny s3:PutBucketPolicy if policy grants Principal "*"
- Enable AWS Config rules: s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited, s3-bucket-public-write-prohibited
- Set up Amazon Macie to classify and monitor sensitive data in S3

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1619 - Cloud Storage Object Discovery
- T1537 - Transfer Data to Cloud Account
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
